{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794250781266,"sessionID":"ses_e3e557db8ffelgfQ3xHuqI1WxJ","part":{"id":"prt_1c1ae321c0015TTpGs801G50IH","messageID":"msg_1c1ae172f0011OdUNQzlG2fFRj","sessionID":"ses_e3e557db8ffelgfQ3xHuqI1WxJ","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794250781267,"sessionID":"ses_e3e557db8ffelgfQ3xHuqI1WxJ","part":{"id":"prt_1c1ae321e0015LpNWevPH6lhK9","messageID":"msg_1c1ae172f0011OdUNQzlG2fFRj","sessionID":"ses_e3e557db8ffelgfQ3xHuqI1WxJ","type":"text","text":"The leaderboard is built, and I tested the backend; I couldn't build the Docker image, because Docker isn't available in this sandbox. I exercised the API through Flask's test client. The checks covered register, login, score submission, rank and personal best, the three periods, player search, admin hide/show, and the 401/403/404/400 error cases. They all behaved as expected. The frontend passes `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build`, but I haven't opened it in a browser.\n\n**Backend (`backend/app.py`)**\n- Data is in SQLite at `data/leaderboard.db`, and passwords are hashed.\n- Login returns a random token, stored hashed and valid for 30 days.\n- The `admin` account has no stored password. It signs in only when `ADMIN_PASSWORD` is set and non-empty, and `admin` can't be registered as a normal user.\n- Usernames must be 3–32 characters (letters, digits, `_`, `.`, `-`) and passwords 6–128 characters. Scores must be integers from 0 to 1,000,000,000,000. These limits are my choice; the spec didn't set any.\n- The leaderboard takes `period` (`all`, `week`, `today`), `limit` (default 50, capped at 100) and `player` (substring match). Players with equal best scores share a rank.\n- The `week` period means the last 7 days, not the calendar week.\n- Non-admin users get 403 on the admin routes, and an unknown score id on toggle gets 404.\n\n**Frontend (`frontend/`)**\n- It has the register and sign-in forms and the username with a sign-out button.\n- The leaderboard has period tabs, search, a refresh button, a 🏆 on the top three and a highlighted row for the signed-in player.\n- The score form shows the new rank and \"New personal best!\".\n- It also lists your recent submissions and best score, and shows the admin an all-scores table with hide/show buttons.\n- It is styled with Tailwind v4 (the only CSS file is `src/index.css`, which just imports Tailwind). I added a `typecheck` script to `package.json`, and the dependencies are in `package-lock.json`.\n- The admin is also shown the score form, so the admin can submit scores like any signed-in player.","time":{"start":1794250781214,"end":1794250781219}}}
